283	/* ══ LIGHT MODE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
284	   Everything in this app resolves through the tokens in @theme, so a light
285	   theme is a token swap rather than a per-component rewrite. `data-theme` is
286	   set on <html> by components/nx/ThemeToggle.tsx and pre-applied by an inline
287	   script in app/layout.tsx so the first paint is already correct.
288	
289	   THE SLATE RAMP IS INVERTED, and that is the load-bearing part. The dark
290	   theme remaps --color-slate-* so the app's ~4,700 existing `text-slate-*`
291	   usages resolve to Nexion's blue-tinted ramp, with 50 lightest and 950
292	   darkest. Body text is `text-slate-300`. Leaving that direction alone in
293	   light mode would paint pale text on a white page. So in light mode the ramp
294	   runs the other way: 50 is the darkest ink and 950 the lightest surface,
295	   which makes `text-slate-300` a readable dark grey and `bg-slate-900` a
296	   near-white panel, with no call site touched.
297	
298	   The ground stays DARKER than the cards here too — the same rule the dark
299	   theme states — so a white card still reads as lifted off the page. */
300	
301	/* `:root:has(.nx-shell-root)[data-theme="light"]`, not bare
302	   `html[data-theme="light"]`: this block re-inverts the SAME tokens
303	   (--color-slate-*, --color-navy-*, --color-brand-*, --color-white) the
304	   dark-mode portal block above (`:root:has(.nx-shell-root) { ... }`,
305	   specificity 0-2-0) already sets — and a bare `html[data-theme="light"]`
306	   is only 0-1-1, so the dark values silently won this fight REGARDLESS of
307	   theme, the whole time, for every plain Tailwind utility built on these
308	   tokens (`text-slate-100`, `text-white`, `bg-navy-900`, …) that never got
309	   its own component-level override. Confirmed live via getComputedStyle by
310	   two independent audits, hitting a WizardStickyCart price, a
311	   WizardReassuranceCard heading, the CookieConsent "Opt out" button, and
312	   the Build-with-AI hero — all rendering the DARK-mode ink/paper values
313	   while `data-theme="light"` was active and visibly not helping. The fix
314	   is the same shape as the dark block's own scoping, plus the attribute
315	   check, which raises this to 0-3-0 — enough to actually win. */
316	:root:has(.nx-shell-root)[data-theme="light"] {
317	  color-scheme: light;
318	
319	  --color-void: #dde5f2;
320	  --color-bg: #e9eff8;
321	  --color-surface: #ffffff;
322	  --color-well: #f3f7fc;
323	  --color-hover: #e8effa;
